      "writtenOn": "2025-02-07T17:21:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, the vdex format is supposed to be as stable as possible. If we reject old vdex files, I can see two major issues:\n\n1. A device that took a Mainline update will not be able to use the old vdex files (assuming Pre-reboot Dexopt hasn\u0027t run), causing huge performance regressions.\n2. Cloud Verification will not work.\n\nCan we avoid bumping the vdex version?",
      "parentUuid": "4b808be6_d5d5fcb2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 126,
        "startChar": 57,
        "endLine": 126,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "fdd45159c7ae097c5b82cf43c926aaeb8a9c39ba",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
